ASSESS:
- Red Force is concentrated with 2 enemy units on the river line and 1 in reserve.
- The urban area provides cover for Red Force units and restricts line of sight.
- The forest on our side offers concealment, but the river acts as a barrier to direct movement.

DEVELOP:
COA A:
- Cross the river using the forested area as cover and surprise Red Force with a flanking maneuver.
- blue-screen: move to (8,6), support_by_fire (8,6) while blue-bridgehead moves to (9,6) to establish a bridgehead.
- blue-support: move to (9,7), attack (9,6) to exploit the bridgehead.

COA B:
- Direct attack on the river line to establish a bridgehead and secure the flank.
- blue-screen: move to (8,7), support_by_fire (8,7) and (9,7) while blue-bridgehead moves to (8,6) and attacks (8,6).
- blue-support: move to (9,8), attack (9,7) to secure the flank.

DETERMINE:
- COA B takes advantage of terrain for cover and follows the doctrinal guidelines of concentration, security, and maneuver.

REASONING:
Following the doctrinal guidelines, we focus on the decisive point (river line) and concentrate combat power there by attacking with all available units. The blue-screen unit will provide security by supporting fire from (8,7) and (9,7), while the blue-bridgehead unit will establish the bridgehead and push into the river line. Blue-support will secure the flank by attacking (9,8) and moving to (9,7) to reinforce the bridgehead.

